      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "Intragastric balloon (IGB) is often used to achieve short-term weight reduction in morbidly obese patients. It is placed endoscopically for a 6-month-period either in the pre-bariatric surgery setting and also in cases where no bariatric surgery is planned. Prolonged implantation may be accompanied by serious complications."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE REPORTS",
          "content": "We herein report two cases of extraction of intact IGBs long time after their placement."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Although no adverse events were observed, adherence to manufacturers' recommendations is definitely suggested."
        }
      ]},
